1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,635
Your rent is due on the first.

2
00:00:03,635 --> 00:00:05,805
Your paycheck lands on a Friday.

3
00:00:05,805 --> 00:00:07,094
Every other Friday.

4
00:00:07,354 --> 00:00:09,087
Or maybe you're a freelancer,

5
00:00:09,087 --> 00:00:11,716
and your income looks like a roller coaster.

6
00:00:11,976 --> 00:00:14,072
The monthly budget advice you've

7
00:00:14,072 --> 00:00:15,774
seen probably doesn't fit.

8
00:00:15,774 --> 00:00:16,429
This will.

9
00:00:16,689 --> 00:00:17,054
Today,

10
00:00:17,054 --> 00:00:18,938
you'll learn how to budget when

11
00:00:18,938 --> 00:00:20,640
you're paid every two weeks,

12
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:23,132
and when your income changes every month.

13
00:00:24,532 --> 00:00:26,479
Welcome back to Broke to Balance.

14
00:00:26,739 --> 00:00:27,546
Quick note:

15
00:00:27,546 --> 00:00:29,014
this is educational,

16
00:00:29,014 --> 00:00:31,216
not personal financial advice.

17
00:00:31,216 --> 00:00:32,684
Let's get organized.

18
00:00:34,084 --> 00:00:35,860
First, know your pay rhythm.

19
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:37,192
It changes your math.

20
00:00:37,452 --> 00:00:38,269
Paid monthly?

21
00:00:38,269 --> 00:00:40,217
That's twelve paychecks a year.

22
00:00:40,217 --> 00:00:41,411
Paid twice a month,

23
00:00:41,411 --> 00:00:43,233
like the first and fifteenth?

24
00:00:43,233 --> 00:00:44,427
That's twenty-four.

25
00:00:44,687 --> 00:00:46,050
Paid every two weeks?

26
00:00:46,050 --> 00:00:47,218
That's twenty-six.

27
00:00:47,218 --> 00:00:48,257
And paid weekly?

28
00:00:48,257 --> 00:00:48,906
Fifty-two.

29
00:00:49,166 --> 00:00:52,073
Twice a month and every two weeks sound the same.

30
00:00:52,073 --> 00:00:52,786
They're not.

31
00:01:00,986 --> 00:01:02,109
Here's the secret.

32
00:01:02,109 --> 00:01:03,732
With twenty-six paychecks,

33
00:01:03,732 --> 00:01:05,668
most months have two paychecks,

34
00:01:05,668 --> 00:01:07,728
but two months a year have three.

35
00:01:07,988 --> 00:01:09,739
Those are your bonus months.

36
00:01:09,739 --> 00:01:11,427
Not a bonus from your boss,

37
00:01:11,427 --> 00:01:13,241
just a quirk of the calendar.

38
00:01:13,501 --> 00:01:14,931
Let's use an example:

39
00:01:14,931 --> 00:01:18,201
fourteen hundred dollars take-home per paycheck.

40
00:01:18,201 --> 00:01:20,721
Budgeting on two paychecks a month is

41
00:01:20,721 --> 00:01:22,696
twenty-eight hundred dollars.

42
00:01:22,956 --> 00:01:25,265
The two extra checks add up to another

43
00:01:25,265 --> 00:01:27,452
twenty-eight hundred dollars a year.

44
00:01:27,452 --> 00:01:29,761
That's real money, if you plan for it.

45
00:01:31,161 --> 00:01:32,047
Strategy one:

46
00:01:32,047 --> 00:01:35,590
build your monthly budget around just two paychecks.

47
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:38,336
Pay your bills and live on those two.

48
00:01:38,336 --> 00:01:40,284
In the three-paycheck months,

49
00:01:40,284 --> 00:01:42,098
the third check is a bonus,

50
00:01:42,098 --> 00:01:43,307
and it gets a job.

51
00:01:43,567 --> 00:01:45,746
Send it to your emergency fund,

52
00:01:45,746 --> 00:01:47,151
extra debt payments,

53
00:01:47,151 --> 00:01:49,611
or a sinking fund for annual bills.

54
00:01:49,871 --> 00:01:50,427
That way,

55
00:01:50,427 --> 00:01:52,405
you never get used to money that

56
00:01:52,405 --> 00:01:54,073
only shows up twice a year.

57
00:01:55,473 --> 00:01:57,866
So what could twenty-eight hundred dollars

58
00:01:57,866 --> 00:01:59,802
of extra paychecks do in one year?

59
00:02:00,062 --> 00:02:03,440
Put one thousand dollars into your emergency fund.

60
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:05,940
Put another one thousand toward debt.

61
00:02:05,940 --> 00:02:09,385
And put eight hundred into a fund for annual bills.

62
00:02:09,645 --> 00:02:12,726
All without touching your normal monthly budget.

63
00:02:12,986 --> 00:02:14,726
That's the power of treating a

64
00:02:14,726 --> 00:02:16,350
calendar quirk as a feature,

65
00:02:16,350 --> 00:02:17,510
not an afterthought.

66
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:19,823
Strategy two:

67
00:02:19,823 --> 00:02:20,946
make a bill map.

68
00:02:21,206 --> 00:02:23,281
List every bill with its due date.

69
00:02:23,281 --> 00:02:25,477
Then match each bill to the paycheck

70
00:02:25,477 --> 00:02:26,880
that arrives before it.

71
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:29,553
Say your first paycheck of the month

72
00:02:29,553 --> 00:02:31,296
covers rent and utilities.

73
00:02:31,296 --> 00:02:33,775
The second covers the car, the phone,

74
00:02:33,775 --> 00:02:34,714
and insurance.

75
00:02:34,974 --> 00:02:36,806
And if a due date is awkward,

76
00:02:36,806 --> 00:02:37,880
call the company.

77
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:40,849
Many will let you move it to match your payday.

78
00:02:42,249 --> 00:02:43,281
Strategy three:

79
00:02:43,281 --> 00:02:44,794
run the fifty, thirty,

80
00:02:44,794 --> 00:02:46,857
twenty rule on every paycheck.

81
00:02:47,117 --> 00:02:48,956
On fourteen hundred dollars,

82
00:02:48,956 --> 00:02:50,992
that's seven hundred for needs,

83
00:02:50,992 --> 00:02:52,437
four twenty for wants,

84
00:02:52,437 --> 00:02:54,801
and two eighty for savings and debt.

85
00:02:55,061 --> 00:02:56,775
It's simple, it's automatic,

86
00:02:56,775 --> 00:02:58,488
and it works no matter which

87
00:02:58,488 --> 00:02:59,957
week the paycheck lands.

88
00:03:01,357 --> 00:03:02,634
Now let's automate it,

89
00:03:02,634 --> 00:03:04,377
so you don't have to remember.

90
00:03:04,637 --> 00:03:06,547
Open a separate bills account.

91
00:03:06,547 --> 00:03:07,311
Each payday,

92
00:03:07,311 --> 00:03:10,367
move that paycheck's share of the bills into it.

93
00:03:10,627 --> 00:03:12,566
Send your savings the same day.

94
00:03:12,566 --> 00:03:15,506
What's left in checking is your spending money,

95
00:03:15,506 --> 00:03:16,945
and it's safe to spend.

96
00:03:18,345 --> 00:03:20,068
Let's turn all of this into a

97
00:03:20,068 --> 00:03:21,672
five-minute payday routine.

98
00:03:21,932 --> 00:03:22,157
One:

99
00:03:22,157 --> 00:03:24,012
move this paycheck's share of the

100
00:03:24,012 --> 00:03:25,698
bills into your bills account.

101
00:03:25,958 --> 00:03:26,193
Two:

102
00:03:26,193 --> 00:03:28,020
send your savings and your debt

103
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:29,257
payment the same day.

104
00:03:29,517 --> 00:03:29,857
Three:

105
00:03:29,857 --> 00:03:32,695
check which bills are due before your next payday.

106
00:03:32,955 --> 00:03:33,269
Four:

107
00:03:33,269 --> 00:03:35,845
glance at what you spent last pay period.

108
00:03:35,845 --> 00:03:38,358
Then you're done, until the next payday.

109
00:03:46,758 --> 00:03:48,296
Now, irregular income.

110
00:03:48,296 --> 00:03:50,602
Never budget off your best month.

111
00:03:50,862 --> 00:03:53,199
Look at the last six to twelve months,

112
00:03:53,199 --> 00:03:56,334
and build your budget around a conservative number,

113
00:03:56,334 --> 00:03:57,625
not your highest one.

114
00:03:57,885 --> 00:03:59,734
Then pay yourself a salary.

115
00:03:59,734 --> 00:04:01,924
All income lands in one account,

116
00:04:01,924 --> 00:04:05,279
and you pay yourself the same amount every month.

117
00:04:05,539 --> 00:04:08,048
Say your income swings between nineteen

118
00:04:08,048 --> 00:04:10,493
hundred and forty-two hundred dollars,

119
00:04:10,493 --> 00:04:12,101
averaging three thousand.

120
00:04:12,101 --> 00:04:14,546
You pay yourself twenty-eight hundred,

121
00:04:14,546 --> 00:04:16,991
with a starter buffer of one thousand.

122
00:04:17,251 --> 00:04:19,399
Slow months dip into the buffer.

123
00:04:19,399 --> 00:04:20,876
Good months refill it.

124
00:04:20,876 --> 00:04:21,950
In this example,

125
00:04:21,950 --> 00:04:25,239
the buffer never drops below six hundred dollars,

126
00:04:25,239 --> 00:04:27,991
and ends the year at thirty-four hundred.

127
00:04:29,391 --> 00:04:31,298
How do you build that starter buffer?

128
00:04:31,558 --> 00:04:33,063
Use your bonus paychecks,

129
00:04:33,063 --> 00:04:34,928
or your best month of the year,

130
00:04:34,928 --> 00:04:36,974
and leave that money in the buffer

131
00:04:36,974 --> 00:04:38,358
instead of spending it.

132
00:04:38,618 --> 00:04:41,685
Aim first for one month of essential expenses.

133
00:04:41,685 --> 00:04:43,952
Then keep growing it toward three.

134
00:04:44,212 --> 00:04:45,155
Once it's full,

135
00:04:45,155 --> 00:04:47,293
your slow months stop being scary.

136
00:04:48,693 --> 00:04:50,993
Irregular costs need a plan too.

137
00:04:50,993 --> 00:04:53,293
Annual insurance, holiday gifts,

138
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:54,443
car maintenance.

139
00:04:54,703 --> 00:04:58,058
Take each yearly cost and divide it by twelve.

140
00:04:58,058 --> 00:05:01,705
Six hundred dollars of insurance is fifty a month.

141
00:05:01,705 --> 00:05:03,893
Four eighty of gifts is forty.

142
00:05:03,893 --> 00:05:06,884
Nine hundred for the car is seventy-five.

143
00:05:07,144 --> 00:05:07,729
Together,

144
00:05:07,729 --> 00:05:10,135
that's one hundred sixty-five dollars

145
00:05:10,135 --> 00:05:11,761
a month in sinking funds,

146
00:05:11,761 --> 00:05:13,842
so those bills never ambush you.

147
00:05:15,242 --> 00:05:16,790
If you're self-employed,

148
00:05:16,790 --> 00:05:18,209
there's one more step:

149
00:05:18,209 --> 00:05:18,596
taxes.

150
00:05:18,856 --> 00:05:20,807
Nobody withholds them for you.

151
00:05:20,807 --> 00:05:22,237
So from every payment,

152
00:05:22,237 --> 00:05:24,448
move a portion into a separate tax

153
00:05:24,448 --> 00:05:26,269
account before you touch it.

154
00:05:26,529 --> 00:05:28,363
How much depends on where you

155
00:05:28,363 --> 00:05:29,881
live and your situation,

156
00:05:29,881 --> 00:05:32,536
so ask a tax professional for your number.

157
00:05:33,936 --> 00:05:35,528
A few common questions.

158
00:05:35,788 --> 00:05:38,393
Can I spend any of the bonus paychecks?

159
00:05:38,393 --> 00:05:40,598
Sure, if your goals are on track.

160
00:05:40,598 --> 00:05:42,001
Many people split it:

161
00:05:42,001 --> 00:05:44,139
most to goals, a little for fun.

162
00:05:44,399 --> 00:05:47,130
What if I have two jobs, or a side hustle?

163
00:05:47,130 --> 00:05:48,756
Put it all in one budget,

164
00:05:48,756 --> 00:05:51,942
and base your fixed bills on the steadier income.

165
00:05:52,202 --> 00:05:54,673
And what if my pay changes mid-year?

166
00:05:54,673 --> 00:05:56,800
Update your numbers right away.

167
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:58,859
A budget is a living document,

168
00:05:58,859 --> 00:05:59,888
not a contract.

169
00:06:01,288 --> 00:06:02,920
Four mistakes to avoid.

170
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:03,423
One:

171
00:06:03,423 --> 00:06:06,037
spending the third paycheck without a plan.

172
00:06:06,297 --> 00:06:06,547
Two:

173
00:06:06,547 --> 00:06:08,675
budgeting off your best month when

174
00:06:08,675 --> 00:06:10,239
your income is irregular.

175
00:06:10,499 --> 00:06:10,920
Three:

176
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,111
having no buffer,

177
00:06:12,111 --> 00:06:14,705
so every slow month becomes a crisis.

178
00:06:14,965 --> 00:06:15,596
And four:

179
00:06:15,596 --> 00:06:16,927
ignoring due dates,

180
00:06:16,927 --> 00:06:18,679
which leads to late fees.

181
00:06:18,679 --> 00:06:20,221
A bill map fixes that.

182
00:06:21,621 --> 00:06:22,691
Let's recap.

183
00:06:22,951 --> 00:06:25,414
Biweekly means twenty-six paychecks.

184
00:06:25,414 --> 00:06:26,918
Budget on two a month,

185
00:06:26,918 --> 00:06:29,107
and give the extra checks a job.

186
00:06:29,367 --> 00:06:31,973
Make a bill map, and automate each payday.

187
00:06:32,233 --> 00:06:33,779
With irregular income,

188
00:06:33,779 --> 00:06:36,801
pay yourself a steady salary from a buffer,

189
00:06:36,801 --> 00:06:40,104
and set aside money for annual bills and taxes.

190
00:06:40,364 --> 00:06:40,930
Remember:

191
00:06:40,930 --> 00:06:43,384
the best budget is the one that matches

192
00:06:43,384 --> 00:06:45,019
how you actually get paid.

193
00:06:45,279 --> 00:06:46,837
If this helped, subscribe,

194
00:06:46,837 --> 00:06:48,515
and tell me in the comments:

195
00:06:48,515 --> 00:06:50,074
how often do you get paid?

196
00:06:50,334 --> 00:06:52,839
And if you learned something from this video,

197
00:06:52,839 --> 00:06:54,899
don't forget to watch our next video.

198
00:06:55,159 --> 00:06:57,717
This video is for education only and

199
00:06:57,717 --> 00:06:59,352
isn't financial advice.

200
00:06:59,352 --> 00:07:00,631
See you next time.

